bs/emperor-go-murakami.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Go-Murakami</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Go-Murakami (1328–1368) was the second emperor of the Southern Court of Japan, reigning from 1339 to 1368 after his father Go-Daigo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-sanjo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-go-sanjo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Go-Sanjō</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Go-Sanjō was the 71st emperor of Japan according to the traditional order of succession, reigning from 1068 to 1073.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-toba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-go-toba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Go-Toba</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Go-Toba was emperor of Japan from 1183 to 1198 and then ruled as retired emperor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-guangwu-of-han"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-guangwu-of-han.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Guangwu of Han</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Guangwu of Han, born Liu Xiu, was a descendant of the Han imperial house who rose against Wang Mang's Xin dynasty and restored the Han in 25 CE, founding the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-huan-of-han"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Huan of Han</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Huan of Han was emperor of the Eastern Han dynasty from 146 to 168.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-huizong"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Huizong</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Huizong was a Northern Song emperor, celebrated as a painter, calligrapher and patron of the arts but criticised for political neglect.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-jing-of-han"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-jing-of-han.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Jing of Han</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Jing of Han, born Liu Qi, was the sixth emperor of the Western Han dynasty, ruling from 157 to 141 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-kanmu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-kanmu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Kanmu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kanmu was emperor of Japan from 781 to 806.</span></a></li></ul>
